{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"0fcc0d16-52b2-4f92-9be8-c149dfb0c30e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Before modifying the code, we queried the `worklore` MCP server using `suggest_for_project` and retrieved relevant story `2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts`.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Fixed Generator ([`gen.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-mEY0xg/gen.py#L10-L14))**:\n   - Replaced key `\"value\"` with `\"start\"` in [`hr_target`](file:///private/tmp/h-mEY0xg/gen.py#L10-L14):\n     ```python\n     def hr_target(step):\n         \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n         lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n         return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n     ```\n\n2. **Documented Rationale ([`ANSWER.md`](file:///private/tmp/h-mEY0xg/ANSWER.md))**:\n   - Recorded the exact modification and the reason: Intervals.icu treats `{value, end}` as a zone-mapped target during Garmin FIT export, causing the watch to clamp ranges to its internal zone bands. Using `{start, end}` switches FIT export to an Instant-HR corridor target that passes the calculated target bounds through directly to the watch without clamping.\n","duration_seconds":40.56776,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":176935,"output_tokens":1515,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":178450}}}
